WEBVTT

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.350
Another new enemy has
shown up to challenge Takao.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:39.620
Dragoon had a really hard time against the Bey's unpredictable movements!

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.160
But that's when...

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.410
We heard Kai's
nostalgic-sounding voice!

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:46.660
Don't forget how you
battle, Takao Kinomiya.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:12.860
Look at this, Takao!

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:16.970
These are the powerful waves that the
Bey was giving off in the battle from earlier.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.490
Is that why it had all those
confusing movements?

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:21.450
It is.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:25.080
I believe that there's some sort of special material inside of the Bey.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.500
So what's this special material then?

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.790
I don't know.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:33.630
If I run an analysis on my footage
I might be able to find something.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.460
As for now, I'm stuck.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.880
I don't care who comes after us!

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.720
'Cause I've got Seiryu with me!

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.810
We'll see if all that
tough talk holds up.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.890
Especially since you were
about to lose that one.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.900
Shut your mouth and keep it shut!

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:56.070
In that case I'm never ever
cheering you on ever again!

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.200
No one ever asked you to!

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.610
What's that supposed to mean?

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:04.410
You're always butting in
where you're not needed!

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:07.120
Why can't you keep
quiet like a girl should?

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.410
You're the last person I
want to hear that from!

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.250
What happened?

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.170
I just found something big!

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.250
The basic structure and
materials of the Bey

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:19.130
mostly match up with the robo-
Blader from the other day!

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.550
The robo-Blader was...

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.470
That was the robot from when we were trapped on that boat, right?

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.140
Which means that...

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:29.770
Takao's opponent today and the bad guys
from back then are in cahoots with each other?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:34.610
I think they're part of the same group. Or at
least he was at a Blader with the same technology.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.110
Darn! Them again?

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:39.570
What a bunch of weird Bladers...

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.220
Why don't I just fight 'em all at once?!

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.870
Someone's just all talk again.

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:46.370
Gimme a break, will ya...

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.620
Regardless!

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:50.160
You shouldn't let
your guard down, Takao.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.710
You can't win with your current fighting
style against our enemies' advanced Beys.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.960
And without Kai's speech,

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:00.550
who knows if you could
have summoned Seiryu?

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:02.550
Now that you say it...

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.560
Speaking of which,
where did Kai go?

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.270
Over there!

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.210
As you can see,

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:22.570
we almost have all
the data we need on

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:27.030
how Takao Kinomiya
summons his Sacred Beast.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:31.250
It's because that Magtram
showed what it could do, yes?

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.210
Right.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.670
But how will the other three fight?

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.250
That's going to be
a problem for us.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.930
You're absolutely right.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:42.860
Takao Kinomiya is not our only target.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:44.690
The strongest team in the world...

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:47.050
The BBA championship team...

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:51.020
Each of their members
has a Sacred Beast.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.940
Are there any updates
on the other three?

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.310
Yes, sir! Kai Hiwatari has
appeared alongside Takao Kinomiya.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.690
As for the remaining two--

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:02.150
We have our positions
set in America and China.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:05.280
We've been keeping our eyes
on them, but no news to report.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.070
It's as he says.

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:10.080
We don't have nearly enough
data on their Sacred Beasts.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.830
We plan on getting men on
the ground there ourselves.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.100
That is far too slow!

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:20.130
That other group has already
made contact with all four of them.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.050
Do you intent to just
stand by and watch them?

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:25.300
We must assemble all four at once.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:29.100
Onto a battlefield where
we have absolute control.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.220
But how are we supposed to...?

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:34.180
I have an idea.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.820
I'm going to rush to find an explanation on what that weird magnetic field was.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:48.500
Yeah. I'm counting on you, Kyoujyu.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:51.450
Hey, Takao. Haven't you
forgotten something?

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:53.040
Forgot something?

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.120
Huh? But Dragoon!

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:55.910
Right here!

00:05:55.910 --> 00:06:00.630
That's not it! You still
haven't introduced us...

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:06.600
Oh, really? My bad.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:08.400
Hey, Kai!

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.930
This is kinda sudden,

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:11.680
but I'll introduce you guys.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.470
She's our classmate.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.890
Hiromi Tachibana. It's nice to meet you!

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:20.560
That's Kai. Get along!

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:23.900
What's with the attitude? How rude.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:26.530
That's how Kai acts to everyone.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:27.860
Don't take it personally.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.450
I will take it personally!

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:32.700
Just who is he, Takao?

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.740
What do you mean "who" is he?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.620
He's a little strange, you could say.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.290
I can tell.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:44.500
Oh, right. Kai, stay at my place tonight!

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.300
Or do you have somewhere else to crash?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.180
Leave me alone.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.570
I knew you'd say that.

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:56.140
I'll talk to grandpa.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.020
So let's go.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.940
C'mon. Don't be shy.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.140
It'll be fine, come on!

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:00.850
Hey!

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.310
Wait, Takao! Gosh...

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.960
I haven't seen you since
the world championships.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:13.160
You've got my respect.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.700
If you consider taking
a break from tops

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.450
and devote yourself to
the way of the sword,

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:20.160
I'm sure you can become
a fine swordsman!

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.670
What do you say?
Want to train under me?

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:34.030
Grandpa, Kai hates it
when people bother him.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:36.220
Mind your own business. Why...

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:40.640
This young man's got far
more focus than you.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:42.810
Swordplay is about the soul!

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:47.480
Speaking of which, you're always
so wishy-washy when it comes to--

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:48.730
Yes, good.

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.990
Save the lectures for later.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:52.410
Later, grandpa!

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:54.740
Hey, Takao! What do you think you're--

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.240
Save it for tomorrow!

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.830
We're done for today!

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:01.580
Goodnight, grandpa!

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:09.210
Let me hear it all tonight, Kai.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:12.760
What were you up to and what
kinds of opponents did you fight?

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.140
Hey, Kai...

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:21.060
Yeah, yeah, I get it.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.100
You're a loner, pure and simple.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.270
What a rowdy family.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:30.990
What's the rush, Hiromi?

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.780
It's too early for this!

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:35.420
It's gotta that Kai-person!

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:37.740
I was up all night thinking about it.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:41.750
Why doesn't he think he's on your side?

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.460
What are you saying?

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:47.170
Kai's our teammate! We fought
all over the world with him!

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:50.640
But he doesn't act like your friend!

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.420
You might think that at first sight, but--

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.760
I think he might be an enemy spy!

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.430
You're totally overthinking it!

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:57.550
How so?!

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.850
Good morning!

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.020
What brings you two here so early?

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:10.940
You see... Um...

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.650
Are you here to warm up with me?

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:16.160
Oh, well that's a relief!

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:18.120
--Let's get you changed, first!
--Hiromi!

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.910
Is Takao here?

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:30.800
Rise and shine, Takao. We need to talk.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.670
I've got a little trick
for waking Takao up.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.180
You're wide open!

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:43.390
Ow...

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:45.850
Awake I see, Takao?

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.270
Grandpa!

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:51.690
Why do you keep waking
me up in weird ways?

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:52.940
Gimme a break--

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:53.860
Takao!

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.540
Hiromi! Kyoujyu!

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.660
Where is he, Takao?

00:09:58.660 --> 00:09:59.630
Who?

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:00.620
Kai.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:02.660
Kai...?

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:06.260
Oh, you're here for Kai?

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:09.500
He said he was going to
take a walk down at the beach.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.250
The beach?

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:16.310
I don't see him.

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:18.300
This is totally suspicious.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.550
Don't be stupid, Hiromi.

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:23.220
There's no way Kai could be a spy.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:26.430
But he never talks about himself.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.730
That's obviously suspicious.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:30.310
You see...

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:50.620
Kai...

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:54.840
As I thought, one of
Ozma's group went to Kai

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:57.590
and had an invisible
Sacred Beast, right?

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:00.220
Yeah.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:19.950
A user of an invisible Sacred Beast?

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:21.910
Then it's just as I thought.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.990
That means we've all lost once.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:27.450
I didn't lose!
It was a draw!

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:28.790
I see.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:30.620
That's nice and all,

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:33.540
but why'd you decide
to come my way?

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:36.640
Well, I started to
miss you a little bit.

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:37.460
Kai...

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.400
Miss your stupid antics, that is.

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:40.630
What's that supposed to mean?

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:44.260
Well, Hiromi? Do you get now that

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:45.800
Kai's one of us?

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:51.940
Kai, I'm sure you understand how frustrated Max, Rei, and I feel.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.270
Let's think of something, together!

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:57.480
Like what we should do to beat
those invisible Sacred Beasts.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:58.860
And a strategy to do it.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:01.570
Kai!

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.910
I'll defeat them myself!

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.740
I don't need your help.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:08.580
Wait up, Kai!

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:13.670
I knew we couldn't trust him.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.430
As far as control over the
Magtram is concerned,

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:28.760
this is a Blader of a much
higher level than Snake.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.060
His name is Daryl.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:32.690
Let's see what you can do, shall we?

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.260
Good afternoon! Pardon me!

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:08.760
"That's all. Please see what you can do."

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.040
It's done!

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:12.310
Good! Now send it off!

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:14.890
What are you doing?

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:17.690
We're asking a favor from Max's mom.

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.320
Max's mom?

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:21.900
Right, you don't know about them.

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:24.490
Max, who's in America,

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:27.070
is another teammate, like Kai.

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:29.740
His mother, Miss Judy,

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:32.540
works for a Beyblade research institution.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.960
What are you asking her for?

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.500
What the material from the other day that emitted a magnetic force was.

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:41.090
I sent her all my data,

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:43.170
so I'm asking her to analyze it for me.

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:46.510
My laptop can only do so much.

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:48.930
Yup. It's a good thing
we had that connection.

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.470
By the way, what brings you here?

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:53.430
I had an idea!

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:57.230
I found an ace in the hole to
help Takao get his revenge.

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:58.060
Huh?

00:13:58.060 --> 00:13:59.020
Really?

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:03.830
Ta-da! I'm going to go ask this person!

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:05.360
That's Chairman Daitenji.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.410
That's the old timer
from the BBA, right?

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:09.370
What about him?

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.330
You're not surprised?

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:12.740
Of course not!

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:14.750
Don't get my hopes up like that.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:17.470
Kyoujyu tried that ages ago.

00:14:17.470 --> 00:14:18.830
Right, Kyoujyu?

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.670
I see.

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.210
This is a great idea!

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:23.220
What?

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:24.420
Right?

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:28.050
If he's a man with a
global network of Bladers,

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:30.800
I thought that he has
to know <b><i>something!</i></b>

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.640
I didn't think of that.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:37.100
C'mon, Kyoujyu, I thought about contacting the ol' coot ages ago!

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:39.690
Then you should have said so!

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:44.780
Dang!

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:47.190
Then let's go right now!

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:48.740
Go where?

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:51.410
Duh!

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:53.830
To the BBA! The BBA!

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:00.400
Representing Team Psykick?

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:06.690
I've put my life on the line to
raise top of the line Bladers.

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:10.060
I would like to put the fruits
of my labor into action.

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:11.800
What do you mean?

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:12.800
In short,

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:18.600
would you allow my players to challenge the BBA championship-winning team?

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:20.350
With them...?

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:24.450
Consider it a title match, I suppose?

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:27.110
We will provide the arena.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:31.070
All you need to do is
assemble the team, Chairman.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.530
But...

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:36.340
I know that they're split up right now.

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:41.500
But fans from all over the world are itching to see them battle again.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:43.710
One moment, please.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:50.510
No offense, but perhaps we should see your players' skill level first?

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:53.180
He's waiting downstairs.

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:55.890
I see you've come prepared.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:02.530
This test match will be one round.

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:05.310
The BBA youth representative

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:08.650
will have a battle against
your representative.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.400
Of course, if you lose,

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:15.710
the request to challenge
the BBA team will be null.

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:17.080
Understood.

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.370
Now, representatives, please step forward.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:19.910
Sir!

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:21.960
Daryl!

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:29.350
We will begin.

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:30.710
Ready?

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.800
Three! Two! One!

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:34.260
Go Shoot!

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:40.930
Excuse me, do you have an
appointment with the Chairman?

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:44.270
Don't worry about it.
The old man and I are cool.

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:45.100
Old man?

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:47.730
This is where the Chairman is, right?

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:52.740
There he is!

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.320
The same face from that magazine!

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.320
Hey, wait!

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:58.950
Hello!

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:13.670
What's the matter? Is that all the BBA youth representative has to offer?

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:24.850
Kyoujyu! Those moves!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:29.050
Yes! It's a perfect match with the other Bey that emitted magnetic waves!

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:30.400
Which means...

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.950
I knew it! There's that
strong magnetic field!

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:37.410
Of course!

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:39.030
Oh, Mr. Kinomiya!

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.790
Wrap it up, Daryl!

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:45.660
Go, Darylanzer!

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:03.350
Team Psykick wins!

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:10.230
You're gonna fight me now!

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:13.400
Don't be so hasty, Mr. Kinomiya.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:15.360
This is a test.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:16.490
A test?

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.700
What do you think, Chairman?

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:22.580
Do you think we have the right to challenge the champion team?

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:26.620
If they can battle like that,
they're plenty qualified.

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:28.640
However...

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:30.670
A challenge to Takao and the team?

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:31.960
I see.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.750
If that's your game,

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:35.550
then I accept, old man!

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:37.310
Mr. Kinomiya...

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:40.180
You heard it here, first!

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:43.760
I started getting pumped
after seeing that battle.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:46.600
You're spouting reckless nonsense again!

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:49.690
Count me in, too.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:51.690
--Kai!

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.440
Mr. Kai Hiwatari...

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:57.900
How enthusiastic.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:03.180
There's half of the
champion team, right there!

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.810
Does that mean we
have a deal, Chairman?

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:07.140
I know.

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:11.830
I will get in contact with Max and Rei.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:13.500
Yes!

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:16.560
The BBA championship
team is back in business!

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:20.340
The BBA officially accepts your challenge,

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:24.640
in a title match against the champions.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:40.320
All of the game pieces
have fallen into place.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:54.380
Takao! It's here!

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:58.510
The analysis I had Miss Judy
do on that magnetic wave!

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:01.470
It's here! Let's see it then!

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:02.630
Here it is.

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:06.720
I don't understand a darn thing!

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.650
You won't unless Kyoujyu explains it.

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:11.390
You're on the slow side.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:12.600
What?!

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.860
Again with the insults...

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:17.270
As for the analysis,

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:19.230
the source of that magnetic wave

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:25.010
It's likely an artifial ore made
by a chemical reaction.

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:26.490
An artificial ore?

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:28.080
Yes. It's just that...

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:33.210
I found that there's an extremely similar naturally occurring ore.

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:38.590
If we put those in our Beys, it's
possible that we can produce similar or...

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:42.720
perhaps even stronger
mangetic waves than they can.

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:44.130
For real?

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:47.440
Will we make it in time
for this next match?

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:50.770
We'll be fine! When Max
arrives in Japan in two days,

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:52.980
she said he'd bring a prototype!

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.060
Awesome! Max's mom
always thinks ahead!

00:20:56.310 --> 00:21:00.230
So what kind of people
are Max and Rei like?

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:01.860
You'll know when you meet them!

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:08.490
Go Shoot!

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:20.210
Takao! This is going to be the first time in a while
that the BBA team has gotten back together!

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:21.170
Yeah.

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:24.800
We can fight together again!

00:22:58.980 --> 00:23:01.480
Max and Rei have arrived in Japan!

00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:03.820
The BBA team is finally back in action!

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:05.400
What's the matter, Chairman?

00:23:05.570 --> 00:23:07.650
Hiromi says "I'm here too"?

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:11.870
So we don't have any choice
but to let her narrate, too?

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:14.700
I can't let that happen! That's my job!

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:17.040
Hey, Hiromi, give me the mic back!

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:18.710
Hiromi, please!

00:23:18.710 --> 00:23:21.210
Just watch the next episode too, okay?
